{"id":"r5","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":5,"of":8,"title":"Letters that change at the end","titleHe":"אוֹתִיּוֹת סוֹפִיּוֹת","goal":"Read ך ם ן ף ץ — the same five letters in their end-of-word shapes.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Five letters are written differently when they finish a word. Same letter, same sound — only the shape changes. Miss them and the alphabet looks like it has twenty-seven letters."},{"type":"finals","items":[{"l":"כ","final":"ך","en":"kaf","name":"כָּף"},{"l":"מ","final":"ם","en":"mem","name":"מֵם"},{"l":"נ","final":"ן","en":"nun","name":"נוּן"},{"l":"פ","final":"ף","en":"pe","name":"פֵּא"},{"l":"צ","final":"ץ","en":"tsadi","name":"צָדִי"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Most of them simply grow a tail that drops below the line. ם is the odd one out: it closes up into a box."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מֶלֶךְ","en":"king","translit":"melech"},{"he":"שָׁלוֹם","en":"peace","translit":"shalom"},{"he":"בֵּן","en":"son","translit":"ben"},{"he":"כֶּסֶף","en":"money, silver","translit":"kesef"},{"he":"עֵץ","en":"tree","translit":"ets"},{"he":"אֶרֶץ","en":"land, country","translit":"erets"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["house","hears","king","specifically, of all things"],"correct":2,"prompt":"מֶלֶךְ","translit":"melech"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to the land","before, not yet","day","peace"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שָׁלוֹם","translit":"shalom"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["correct","blessing","friend (m.)","son"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֵּן","translit":"ben"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tree","good","money, silver","window"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כֶּסֶף","translit":"kesef"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tree","goes, walks","three (m.)","sometimes"],"correct":0,"prompt":"עֵץ","translit":"ets"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["one (m.)","five (m.)","reads","land, country"],"correct":3,"